# E05 English auction without broadcast: parallel; the valuations come from the seed of the oracle, and each bidder only
# talks to the auctioneer. Compared: the valuations and the result, the messages each bidder receives in order, and
# all the messages as a multiset (the only fact that shows the name of a sender). When the last price gets no bid, the
# C# sells to the first bid of the round before, whose bidder has stopped meanwhile and never prints that it won:
# with two bidders at that price, which one wins depends on the order of arrival, in the C# as in the C++; no two
# bidders tie at the seed of the oracle.
# A sender removed before its last messages are read is shown by its identifier in the C++ (a known divergence of
# the library): "alias" pairs such a message with its C# counterpart, equal on every other column.
ignore ^$
cover all
fact valuation ^\[(bidder\d+)\]: My valuation is (\d+)$
fact finished ^\[auctioneer\]: Auction finished\. (.*)$
fact won ^\[(bidder\d+)\]: I have won\.$
fact to_bidder ^\t\[\w+ -> (bidder\d+)\]: (.*)$
fact message ^\t\[(\w+) -> (\w+)\]: (.*)$
same valuation bag
same finished seq
optional won
same won seq
same to_bidder seq by 0
same message bag alias 0 ^[A-Za-z0-9]{15}$
check valuation count == 5
check finished count == 1
